          "id": "a-midsummer-nights-dream-1-2-line-0029",
          "number": 29,
          "speechLineNumber": 1,
          "text": "And I may hide my face, let me play Thisbe too. I'll speak in a monstrous little voice; 'Thisne, Thisne!'—'Ah, Pyramus, my lover dear! thy Thisbe dear! and lady dear!'",
          "plainText": "And I may hide my face let me play Thisbe too I'll speak in a monstrous little voice 'Thisne Thisne''Ah Pyramus my lover dear thy Thisbe dear and lady dear'",
